# Copy this file to `.env` (in this same directory) and put your real values there.
# `.env` is gitignored — your real keys never get committed.
# This file is the template — keep the placeholder values below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BYOK (client-direct Groq call) — used by users on the no-account tier.
# Get a free key at https://console.groq.com/keys
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GROQ_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (Free hosted + Pro tiers). Tauri client uses these to:
#   1. Open the OAuth login in a browser, then redirect to the deep link.
#   2. POST to the /enhance edge function with the user's JWT.
#
# The ANON key is safe to ship in the client — it's row-level-security gated.
# Never put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY here; that key belongs only in the
# Supabase function's secret store (set via `supabase secrets set ...`).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Vite-exposed mirrors of SUPABASE_URL/SUPABASE_ANON_KEY. Same values,
# different consumer: Vite only ships VITE_-prefixed env vars to the
# browser bundle (the Supabase JS client lives in src/lib/supabase.ts).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Edge function secrets (NOT loaded by the desktop app; set in Supabase
# project secrets via `supabase secrets set HOSTED_GROQ_API_KEY=...`).
# Listed here only as a reminder of which secrets the function expects.
#
#   HOSTED_GROQ_API_KEY      — Groq key the function uses on behalf of users
#   SUPABASE_URL             — auto-injected by Supabase runtime
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — auto-injected by Supabase runtime
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
